# Media proxy configuration (server-side only).
#
# The Express server proxies catalog and playback metadata from a
# self-hosted MovieBox-compatible media worker (the reference API is the
# "Spün MovieBox API" Cloudflare Worker — https://github.com/heisdanny64/spun-moviebox-api).
# Set these in your shell, or in apps/server/.env — the server loads
# apps/server/.env automatically (dotenv), and shell variables take
# precedence over the file:
#
#   MEDIA_API_BASE_URL=https://your-worker.workers.dev
#   MEDIA_API_SECRET=your-worker-secret
#
# Requirements:
#   - MEDIA_API_BASE_URL is the worker root URL. The proxy appends the
#     worker's root-level routes (/home, /search, /info/:subjectId,
#     /season/:subjectId, /stream/:subjectId) — do NOT add an /api/v1
#     prefix; the worker does not serve one.
#   - MEDIA_API_SECRET must match the secret the worker operator configured
#     as its auth secret (MOVIEBOX_SECRET on the reference worker). It is
#     sent as the X-Worker-Secret header and never leaves this server.
#
# When unset, the server still runs but media endpoints respond with
# 503 MEDIA_NOT_CONFIGURED. Credentials never reach the browser.
#
# Quick verification once configured:
#   curl -s http://localhost:4000/api/v1/health
#   curl -s http://localhost:4000/api/v1/media/home
MEDIA_API_BASE_URL=
MEDIA_API_SECRET=

# ── Optional: TMDB secondary metadata provider ───────────────────────────────
#
# TMDB (https://developer.themoviedb.org/) is used ONLY as a secondary
# metadata/discovery provider: when the primary MovieBox provider fails
# (e.g. an upstream outage), search and details fall back to TMDB metadata.
#
#   TMDB_API_KEY=<server-side key>
#
# Requirements / guarantees:
#   - The key is read from the server environment only. NEVER expose it to
#     the browser (no VITE_-prefixed variable).
#   - TMDB is optional: without a key, Zen-Stream behaves exactly as before.
#   - MovieBox remains the primary provider; TMDB never replaces it.
#   - TMDB is metadata/discovery only — playback NEVER comes from TMDB.
#     TMDB titles always normalize to hasResource:false, so they can never
#     become playable through the availability model.
#   - TMDB rate limits (429) and failures surface as the standard
#     MEDIA_UPSTREAM_ERROR, never as "no results".
TMDB_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: Spün secondary metadata provider ────────────────────────────────
#
# Spün (https://spün.xyz) is a metadata/discovery companion used for search
# and details fallback. It is registered whenever the server runs — no key
# is required.
#
#   SPUN_MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://media.byspun.xyz/v1
#
# Guarantees:
#   - Metadata/discovery only — playback NEVER comes from Spün. Spün titles
#     always normalize to hasResource:false, so they can never become
#     playable through the availability model.
#   - Spün identity lookups (/utility/resolve) are cached for 24 hours;
#     failed lookups are never cached.
#   - Failures surface as MEDIA_UPSTREAM_ERROR, never as "no results".
SPUN_MEDIA_BASE_URL=

# ── Optional: DaraTech secondary metadata provider ────────────────────────────
#
# DaraTech (https://apimovie.runflix.name.ng) is a secondary metadata/
# discovery provider for search and details fallback. Register it by setting
# a server-side API key:
#
#   DARATECH_BASE_URL=https://apimovie.runflix.name.ng   # or .../v1 (normalized)
#   DARATECH_API_KEY=<your server-side key>
#
# Guarantees:
#   - The key is read from the server environment only. NEVER expose it to
#     the browser (no VITE_-prefixed variable). The key is NEVER committed —
#     this file only carries a placeholder.
#   - Metadata/discovery only — playback NEVER comes from DaraTech; its
#     titles always normalize to hasResource:false. DaraTech's stream
#     endpoints are NOT integrated, and Zen-Stream never bypasses
#     access controls (e.g. user-agent spoofing) to reach them.
#   - DaraTech ids are deterministic: base64(<numeric MovieBox id>:::pica).
#   - Failures (401/403/429/5xx) surface as MEDIA_UPSTREAM_ERROR, never as
#     "no results". Without the key, DaraTech is simply not registered.
DARATECH_BASE_URL=
DARATECH_API_KEY=